# QGroundControl Debugging and Logging

## Logging Categories
Define logging categories in each source file:
```cpp
QGC_LOGGING_CATEGORY(MissionServiceLog, "MissionServiceLog")
QGC_LOGGING_CATEGORY(MissionUploadServiceLog, "MissionUploadServiceLog")
QGC_LOGGING_CATEGORY(PtahMissionGeneratorLog, "PtahMissionGeneratorLog")
```

## Debug Logging Patterns
```cpp
// Function entry logging
qCDebug(MissionServiceLog) << "GenCall1: FunctionName() - Description";

// Parameter logging
qCDebug(MissionServiceLog) << "Parameters: waypoints=" << waypoints.size() 
                          << "altitude=" << altitude;

// Coordinate logging
qCDebug(MissionServiceLog) << "Coordinate:" << coordinate.toString();

// Error logging
qCWarning(MissionServiceLog) << "Error: Invalid parameter provided";
```

## GenCall Numbering System
Use sequential GenCall numbers to trace execution flow:
- GenCall1: Function entry
- GenCall2: Parameter validation
- GenCall3: Main logic
- GenCall4: Result processing
- GenCall5: Signal emission

## QML Debugging
```qml
// QML debug logging
console.log("GenCall1: QML function entry");
console.log("Parameters:", waypointCount, altitude);
console.log("Signal received:", success);
```

## Common Debug Points
- **Function Entry**: Log when entering major functions
- **Parameter Validation**: Log input parameters and validation results
- **Coordinate Operations**: Log all coordinate calculations and results
- **Vehicle Operations**: Log vehicle assignments and mission uploads
- **Signal Emission**: Log when signals are emitted
- **Error Conditions**: Log all error conditions and fallbacks

## Debug Output Format
```
default:: 34.445 - debug: GenCall26: PtahMissionGenerator::calculateMiddlePoint() - Calculating center point
default:: 34.445 - debug: GenCall27: Calculating average latitude and longitude
default:: 34.445 - debug: GenCall28: PtahMissionGenerator::generateCoordinatesInBothDirections() - Generating waypoint grid
```

## Testing Patterns
- Test with different waypoint counts (5, 10, 20)
- Test with different altitudes (5m, 10m, 15m)
- Test with different vehicle counts (1, 2, 3)
- Verify waypoint sequence is sequential
- Verify altitude separation between drones
- Verify special mission for drone ID 1